# Memory security

Never write secrets into `AGENTS.md`, `PROJECT.md`, `.cursor/state/*`, commits, skill outputs, or **ai-memory** wiki / observations.

## Secrets include

API keys, tokens, passwords, private keys, OAuth refresh material, connection strings with credentials, `.env` values, session cookies.

## If a secret appears

1. Do not copy it into memory files or the wiki
2. Tell the user to rotate it
3. Redact any accidental paste in the same turn
4. If it may already be in ai-memory storage, tell the user to purge/redact via upstream lifecycle docs — do not re-store

## Safe to store

Tool names, non-secret paths, stack choices, approved decisions, durable prefs without credentials.
